WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.477
Run the contact-data quality project.

00:00:02.477 --> 00:00:05.337
Focus on one output column at a time.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:07.737
Compare raw and clean names.

00:00:07.737 --> 00:00:11.032
Check how email normalization affects the domain.

00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:14.732
Look at the email status field and address replacement.

00:00:14.732 --> 00:00:21.147
The goal is to make data-quality decisions visible rather than silently modifying the source.

00:00:21.147 --> 00:00:26.152
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:30.427
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:34.682
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:34.682 --> 00:00:39.792
In a real setting such as a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates,

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:44.702
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:47.507
before discussing syntax.

00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:53.680
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
